# Opening Settings -> Wi-Fi, so that something asks the radio to scan.
#
# Nothing scans on its own: iOS lists networks only while the Wi-Fi pane is open -- wifid asks
# apple80211 for a scan, the reference implementation's lx layer hands it to ath11k, and the firmware
# answers. The touches are the ones rc.jobs.launch already proved on this port: a swipe from the
# bottom edge dismisses the lock screen, then a tap on the Settings icon at (0.615, 0.71). The first
# attempt (wifiscan, 13:39) tapped at 20 s without the swipe, while the lock screen was still up,
# and nothing happened.
#
#   40 s  the lock screen goes away
#   46 s  Settings
#   52 s  the Wi-Fi row, the second row of the first group
#   then  a tap in the middle of the list every 20 s, which a scan result does not mind: the pane
#         stays open and awake until the run ends
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200 wait 6 tap 0.615 0.71 wait 6 tap 0.5 0.25
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20 tap 0.5 0.55
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20 tap 0.5 0.55
